{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"evolvable-sooty-okapi","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_split_jql_queries.py` fails 3 of 3 nodes\n(`ValueError: inbound fetch requires a valid jira.project key ... got ''`, raised from\n`fetcher.jql_active` via `_build_snapshot`) when, on ONE pytest process, it runs after\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` AND at least one test outside\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` (even an empty one). It passes alone, passes after either file\nalone, and passed in `make verify` / CI's default order (where it collects before the\nhardening module).\n\nMinimal reproduction (serial, `-p no:randomly`), reproduced on origin/main 5ad259f2c75 and on\n441ca94f4a8:\n\n```\npytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py \\\n       <any tests/unit/test_*.py outside rebar_reconciler> \\\n       tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_split_jql_queries.py -p no:randomly -q\n```\n\n## Mechanism (confirmed by a controlled substitution)\n\nEvery node of the hardening module triggers it, so it is the module's import:\n`test_wiki_render_hardening.py` loads `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`, whose\nimport runs `sys.path.insert(0, str(ENGINE_ROOT))` (`src/rebar/_engine`) and never removes it.\nA throwaway module under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` containing ONLY that `sys.path.insert`\nreproduces the 3 failures with the same probe and V; without it, 0. Not yet established: which\nmodule then resolves to a second copy through the extra path entry once the\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` conftest scope is torn down and re-entered.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`make test` and CI run `-n 4 --dist worksteal`; work stealing can place this order on one\nworker, so this is a latent order-dependent failure even though no CI run has shown it.\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\nStop the generator import from mutating `sys.path` persistently when imported as a test helper\n(restore it, or import the engine package the same way the test suite does), and add the\nminimal reproduction above as a regression test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The minimal reproduction passes (0 failures in the fetcher module).\n- [ ] Importing the generator from a test leaves `sys.path` unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py tests/unit/test_logging_level.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_split_jql_queries.py -p no:randomly -q\n```","id":"0796-3fa4-8d7d-47aa","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["test-isolation"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Importing generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs from a test leaves src/rebar/_engine on sys.path, so test_fetcher_split_jql_queries fails after it in some orders"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792411775346203001,"uuid":"6da71edf-feec-4861-812e-aef91b8b1729"}